 "skillDocs": {
  "visual-brand-foundation": {
   "content": "---\nname: visual-brand-foundation\ndescription: Develop a coherent visual brand identity and an applied brand or CI sheet.\nlicense: MIT\n---\n\n# Visual Brand Foundation\n\nBuild a brand system that holds together across product, print and social. Start from what exists; do not invent a new brand when the brief asks for a refresh.\n\n## When to use\n\n- A product needs a **CI sheet**: logo direction, typography, colour roles, motifs.\n- An existing identity feels inconsistent and needs rules.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Collect references: the product, competitors, the brief.\n2. Define **colour roles** (primary, surface, ink, accent) before picking hex values.\n3. Pick two type families at most; set a scale with `clamp()`.\n4. Apply everything to three representative screens.\n\n| Role | Light | Dark |\n|---|---|---|\n| Surface | `#ffffff` | `#181818` |\n| Ink | `#1a1c1f` | `#ffffff` |\n| Accent | `#0285ff` | `#339cff` |\n\n```css\n:root { --accent: #0285ff; --radius: 12px; }\n```\n\nSee `references/typography.md` for the type scale.\n",
